div.p:
A. Government position is bifurcated one. On the one hand it offers free and
                    honest elections, while on other hand it steps up level of violence and
                    repression;

C. Parties of moderate opposition have tried to point up for GOES the road toward
                    better relations and acceptable electoral climate; in return they have been
                    threatened by “Mano Blanca”;

D. In Church meeting with parties of moderate opposition and enlightened elements
                    of private sector, agreement has been reached on five indispensable elements for
                    free election;

E. If GOES were to comply with points (1) through (5) it would create a climate
                    permitting necessary discussions. Moderate opposition has made these
                    requirements known publicly through its “popular forum”;
